diff --git a/runtime/README.md b/runtime/README.md
index 61794a2c2d38a83dd69da57805a40e9c526d4530..21d11119708979afd642356314f631eb060ff46d 100644
--- a/runtime/README.md
+++ b/runtime/README.md
@@ -590,6 +590,8 @@ $env:LEONIDA_VK_VALIDATION = '1'
 On a Windows Vulkan build, configure CMake with `-DLEONIDA_TEST_GUEST_DRAW=ON` and build the
 `tiny_guest_draw` and `gta6rt` targets. With llvm-mc, spirv-as and spirv-val available at configure
 time, run `ctest --test-dir runtime/build -C Release -R "^d3d12_translated_draw_guest$" -V`.
+For a Unix-to-Windows cross-build, configure with `-DCMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING_EMULATOR=wine`
+and run the same CTest command with the Wine prefix that can access the build tree.
 The loader maps the test executable. It imports the Xbox device factory, submits three draws using two
 handwritten shaders, reads back a 64×64 offscreen texture and checks every pixel.
 
diff --git a/runtime/test/run_guest_draw.cmake b/runtime/test/run_guest_draw.cmake
